WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.360
Application security matters because software now sits directly in front of customer data,

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:07.140
business workflows, and internal systems.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:11.920
A small weakness in authorization, input handling, configuration,

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:16.860
or monitoring can become a path to data exposure, operational disruption,

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:18.600
or loss of trust.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:23.220
Compliance matters because it gives organizations a repeatable way to describe security

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.720
expectations,

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:28.780
assign responsibilities, and prove that safeguards are being managed.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.160
It does not replace engineering judgment,

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:35.220
but it helps teams avoid treating security as a set of disconnected tasks.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.520
OWASP is a community-driven source of application security guidance.

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:45.020
The OWASP Top 10 gives teams a shared vocabulary for the most common and consequential web

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.160
application risk categories,

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:51.140
making it easier to prioritize review, testing, and remediation.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:58.160
NIST SP 800-53 Rev. 5 is a catalog of security and privacy controls used across federal,

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:01.340
regulated, and risk-focused environments.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:06.360
Its control families cover areas such as access control, audit and accountability,

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:11.460
configuration management, incident response, risk assessment, system integrity,

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:13.520
and system development.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:18.860
This course pairs each OWASP Top 10 risk with attack examples, practical mitigations,

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:23.240
and selected NIST SP 800-53 controls.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:26.180
The goal is not to claim automatic compliance,

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.240
but to help technical teams connect vulnerability work to control intent.

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:34.380
Use OWASP categories to organize application risk discussions.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:39.720
Use NIST controls to connect technical work to governance, evidence, and accountability.

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:43.380
Treat mappings as guidance that still requires local validation.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:48.800
Selected NIST mappings for this topic include SA-3 - System Development Life Cycle;

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:53.900
RA-3 - Risk Assessment; PM-9 - Risk Management Strategy.
